{"type":"p","text":"Neural Sensors"},{"type":"p","text":"BCI"},{"type":"p","text":"Real-Time Signal Processing"}]},{"heading":"Target Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate should be able to take neural data through the complete analytical pipeline:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Neural Recording","Data Acquisition","Signal Quality Check","Filtering","Artifact Removal","Epoching","Feature Extraction","Statistical Analysis","Machine Learning","Neural Decoding","Performance Evaluation","BCI / Research Application"]},{"type":"p","text":"They should be able to explain what the signal represents, how it was processed, why the chosen features are appropriate, and whether the model genuinely generalizes."}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For B.Tech/B.E. — Neuro-Engineering / Brain-Computer Interfaces, the strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Signal Processing Engineer","ML Engineer","Neurotechnology Specialist"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should prioritize DSP, Python/MATLAB, statistics, EEG analysis, machine learning and neuroscience fundamentals."},{"type":"p","text":"For a future-ready profile, the strongest combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Digital Signal Processing","EEG/BCI","Python/MATLAB","Machine Learning","Neural Decoding","Real-Time Systems."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"For advanced research-oriented neural interfaces, a relevant M.Tech/M.S. and potentially Ph.D. can become important, particularly for invasive BCI and novel neural-interface research."}]}]}